{
  "requirement": "Listing and reading failures return errors, distinct from successful empty\nlistings and successful reads of empty files.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.sources.provider.errors`. The requirement has two obligations: listing and reading failures return errors, and those errors are distinct from successful empty listings and successful empty reads.\n\n**Failures return errors**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/tests.rs#fn[failed_provider_operations_never_become_successful_empty_results]` uses `FailingProvider`. Its `list` fails when `list_fails` is set, and its `read` always fails. The test runs with `list_fails` both true and false.\n  - `search_text` must return the matching error, \"listing failed\" or \"reading failed\".\n  - `parse` must return \"reading failed\".\n  - `search_structure` must return the matching error.\n  - The `.err().expect(...)` calls and exact message assertions prove the failure is not turned into an empty success.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/tests.rs#fn[completeness_is_false_only_when_a_match_is_omitted_and_errors_propagate]` adds that an invalid pattern gives an error. Invalid UTF-8 bytes and an unknown language each make `parse_snapshot` return an error.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[empty_sources_errors_and_retained_snapshots_remain_distinct]` covers the real filesystem `Sources`:\n  - `list` errors when the root is a file.\n  - `list` errors when the root is missing.\n  - `list` errors for a missing scope.\n  - `read` errors for a missing file, for `../` paths, and for an absolute path.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[scoped_inspection_skips_unrelated_directories_and_reports_relevant_ignore_errors]` shows `list` and `read` return errors for a broken `.gitignore`. On unix, `list` also errors for a symlink.\n\n**Distinct from successful empty results**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/tests.rs#fn[successful_empty_listing_and_empty_resources_are_distinct_from_errors]` uses `Primitives` with an empty listing and with a one-item listing of an empty file.\n  - `list` returns `Ok` with the expected length.\n  - `read` and `parse` return `Ok` with empty bytes.\n  - `search_text` and `search_structure` return `Ok` with `complete` true and no matches.\n- In the `Sources` test, an empty directory lists as `Ok` and empty. The test also reads an empty file successfully, with empty bytes.\n\nThe error cases and the empty-success cases are checked against each other, in both the provider-level and filesystem tests, and the assertions check the outcomes. I found no gap.",
  "references": "4b9203b0a488dc4487cc9c5b785258007920be5ad703e2cd52ebadf5d9e380bc",
